<title>SURINAM: GOVERNMENT LIST.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT LIST.</headline>
<text>
<p>SURINAM GOVERNMENT LIST (960906)</p>
<p>President (sworn in 16 Sept 91 for</p>
<p>	5-year term)......................Ronald VENETIAAN (NPS)</p>
<p>Vice-President (sworn in 16 Sept 91</p>
<p>	for 5-year term).....................Jules AJODHIA (VHP)</p>
<p>				 - - - - - - -</p>
<p>President-elect (to be sworn in 14 Sept</p>
<p>	for 5-year term).................Jules WIJDENBOSCH (NDP)</p>
<p>Vice-President-elect (to be sworn in 14 Sept</p>
<p>	for 5-year term)................Pretaab RADAKISHUN (NDP)</p>
<p>				 - - - - - - -</p>
<p>OUTGOING GOVERNMENT: (Formed 17 Sep 91)</p>
<p>MINISTERS:</p>
<p>  Agriculture &amp; Husbandry...................Johan SISIL (KTPI)</p>
<p>  Defence................................Siegfried GILDS (SPA)</p>
<p>  Education &amp; Science.......................Gerard HIWAT (NPS)</p>
<p>  Finance............................Humphrey HILDENBERG (NPS)</p>
<p>  Foreign Affairs..........................Subhas MUNGRA (VHP)</p>
<p>  Health.................................Rakied KUDHABUX (VHP)</p>
<p>  Internal Affairs........................Saban SABIRAN (KTPI)</p>
<p>  Justice &amp; Police....................Soeshiel GIRJASING (VHP)</p>
<p>  Labour......................................Jack KROSS (SPA)</p>
<p>  Natural Resources.........................Franco DEMON (NPS)</p>
<p>  Planning..................................Ronald ASSEN (NPS)</p>
<p>  Public Works..................Radjkoemar RANDJIETSINGH (VHP)</p>
<p>  Regional Development..................Romeo VAN RUSSEL (NPS)</p>
<p>  Social Affairs..........................Willy SOEMITA (KTPI)</p>
<p>  Trade &amp; Industry........................Richard KALLOE (VHP)</p>
<p>  Transport, Communications &amp; Tourism.......John DEFARES (SPA)</p>
<p>				  - - - - - - - -</p>
<p>PARTY AFFILIATIONS:</p>
<p>NDP  -- National Democratic Party</p>
<p>NPS  -- National Party of Surinam</p>
<p>SPA  -- Surinamese Labour Party</p>
<p>VHP  -- Progressive Reformation Party</p>
<p>KTPI -- Party of Ethical Standards</p>
<p>				  - - - - - - - -</p>
<p>  Central Bank President.........................Andre TELTING</p>
<p>				  - - - - - - - -</p>
